From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:04:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(miniwin): name the primary DirectDraw driver "display"

DirectDrawEnumerate passed a null driver name, which a program that
prints the description and name together shows as "(null)". Windows
names the primary display driver "display".

diff --git a/miniwin/src/ddraw/ddraw.cpp b/miniwin/src/ddraw/ddraw.cpp
index 4e0b622..dbefeab 100644
--- a/miniwin/src/ddraw/ddraw.cpp
+++ b/miniwin/src/ddraw/ddraw.cpp
@@ -528,7 +528,10 @@ HRESULT DirectDrawEnumerate(LPDDENUMCALLBACKA cb, void* context)
 {
 	const char* driverName = SDL_GetCurrentVideoDriver();
 	char* driverNameDup = SDL_strdup(driverName);
-	BOOL callback_result = cb(NULL, driverNameDup, NULL, context);
+	// The primary driver's name is "display", as on Windows: programs print
+	// the description and the name together.
+	char displayName[] = "display";
+	BOOL callback_result = cb(NULL, driverNameDup, displayName, context);
 	SDL_free(driverNameDup);
 	if (!callback_result) {
 		return DDERR_GENERIC;
